      "reviewNotes": [
        "All 44 paper pages and all 24 native scheme pages visually swept. Paper pages 7, 9, 21 and 23 contain only continuation working grids; pages 42–43 are additional work and page 44 the back cover. Question sources retain every task, diagram, table and labelled graph template. Scheme solutions occupy pages 6–17; pages 19–21 contain general modelling-project assessment rubrics, not additional tasks printed in this examination paper.",
        "All 51 canonical tasks and tariffs match. Q2(b) separates the two velocities at 25/5 including the shared equations in the first task. Q5(a)(i) marks both force diagrams at 5 each. Q8(iii) marks the two velocities at 5 each. Q6(i) and Q10(a)(i) retain each required pair of recurrence values under one 5-mark response. Q9(ii) earliest/latest event times form one 20-mark network response. No additional distinct translated task or finite optional pool."
